# Contract Management System - Cursor Rules

## 🔐 Authentication & Keycloak
- ALWAYS use Keycloak for authentication
- NEVER bypass authentication layers
- ALWAYS sync users to Keycloak before testing
- Use service APIs, never direct database calls
- Test authentication after ANY changes
- Use `./fix-auth.sh` for authentication issues

## 🏗️ Development Workflow
- Test current state before making changes
- Make small, focused changes
- Test immediately after each change
- Don't move on until it's working
- Use `npm run status` to check system health
- Document all configuration changes

## 🧪 Testing Requirements
- Test login after every change
- Verify all user roles work (TDC, TDP, CCRP, AppAdmin)
- Check API endpoints respond correctly
- Validate environment file sync
- Run health checks before and after changes

## 📝 Documentation
- Update docs when making changes
- Document any manual steps required
- Keep troubleshooting guide current
- Note any workarounds or fixes
- Use clear commit messages with context

## 🔧 Automation
- Use `./fix-auth.sh` for authentication issues
- Use `./start-system.sh` for full system startup
- Use `npm run status` to check system health
- Use `npm run test:login` to test authentication
- Use `cd backend && node auto-fix-keycloak.js` for Keycloak issues

## 🚨 Common Issues & Solutions
- "Invalid client credentials" → Run `./fix-auth.sh`
- "Realm not found" → Run `cd backend && node auto-fix-keycloak.js`
- "User not synced" → Run `npm run keycloak:sync`
- Backend won't start → Check port usage and restart
- Environment issues → Sync .env and config.env files

## 📋 Development Checklist
For Every Change:
- [ ] Test current state before changes
- [ ] Make small, focused changes
- [ ] Test immediately after each change
- [ ] Verify related functionality still works
- [ ] Update documentation if needed
- [ ] Commit with clear, descriptive message

For Authentication Changes:
- [ ] Test login before changes
- [ ] Make the change
- [ ] Run `./fix-auth.sh` if needed
- [ ] Test login after changes
- [ ] Verify all user types work
- [ ] Check API endpoints

## 🎯 Best Practices
- Always test authentication after changes
- Use automated scripts when available
- Document any manual steps required
- Keep environment files in sync
- Use persistent Keycloak configuration
- Monitor system health regularly 